# Solar System Explorer

Interactive 3D solar system built with Three.js, custom GLSL shaders, and a PHP JSON API backend, plus a parallel set of X3D models. Built for the Web 3D assignment (2026).

**Live:** http://users.sussex.ac.uk/~mm2505/

## Features

- Real-time 3D scene (Three.js) with orbit controls, adjustable animation speed, and toggleable orbit rings, labels, wireframe, and bloom
- Custom vertex/fragment GLSL shaders for the Sun (surface noise) and planet atmospheres (fresnel-style rim glow), instead of default Three.js materials
- Post-processing pipeline (`EffectComposer` + `RenderPass` + `UnrealBloomPass`) with tuned bloom threshold, strength, and exposure
- PHP backend serving planet metadata through a small model/controller JSON API (`api.php`)
- Dual 3D formats: the live Three.js scene, plus standalone X3D model files under `models/x3d/` for each planet
- Procedural scene build: a Python + Blender script (`models/build_solar_system.py`) constructs the scene and materials, and `generate_x3d.py` exports the X3D models, keeping both formats in sync
- Responsive Bootstrap layout with accessibility support (skip link, ARIA labels, visible focus states)

## Structure

```
css/       stylesheet
js/        Three.js scene, controls, shaders
php/       backend model + JSON API endpoint
models/    Blender source, build/export scripts, X3D model files
index.html      home / 3D scene
explore.html     explore view
about.html       references and write-up
submission.html  assignment submission details
```

## Running locally

The app fetches modules and textures over HTTP, so it needs to be served rather than opened as a local file:

```
php -S localhost:8000
```

Then visit `http://localhost:8000/index.html`.

## Tech

Three.js, GLSL, PHP, Bootstrap 5, Blender/Python (asset pipeline).
